@.str.21 = private unnamed_addr constant [930 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Upgrade Nix to the stable version declared in Nixpkgs:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix upgrade-nix\0A  ```\0A\0A* Upgrade Nix in a specific profile:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix upgrade-nix --profile ~alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command upgrades Nix to the stable version.\0A\0ABy default, the latest stable version is defined by Nixpkgs, in\0A[nix-fallback-paths.nix](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/raw/master/nixos/modules/installer/tools/nix-fallback-paths.nix)\0Aand updated manually. It may not always be the latest tagged release.\0A\0ABy default, it locates the directory containing the `nix` binary in the `$PATH`\0Aenvironment variable. If that directory is a Nix profile, it will\0Aupgrade the `nix` package in that profile to the latest stable binary\0Arelease.\0A\0AYou cannot use this command to upgrade Nix in the system profile of a\0ANixOS system (that is, if `nix` is found in `/run/current-system`).\0A\0A\00", align 1
